From: 1q9lugp <lackowork84@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:58:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/27] v3d: no buffer-texture acceleration on V3D 3.x

Lets Mesa take the CPU PBO upload path, which is correct: all
teximage2d_pbo and texsubimage2d_pbo GLES3 cases pass.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_screen.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_screen.c b/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_screen.c
index eb41579..c7e509d 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_screen.c
@@ -302,7 +302,11 @@ v3d_screen_get_param(struct pipe_screen *pscreen, enum pipe_cap param)
                 return screen->prim_types;
 
         case PIPE_CAP_TEXTURE_BUFFER_OBJECTS:
-                return true;
+                /* 3.x buffer views cannot back Mesa's accelerated PBO
+                 * upload path; reporting them causes a sampler NULL crash
+                 * and corrupt texture contents. Mesa's CPU PBO path is
+                 * correct until 3.x buffer-view sampling is implemented. */
+                return screen->devinfo.ver >= 40;
 
         case PIPE_CAP_TEXTURE_BUFFER_OFFSET_ALIGNMENT:
                 return V3D_TMU_TEXEL_ALIGN;
